{
    "background_story": "Hannah was a marine biologist who spent most of her career studying the majestic sea creatures of New Zealand. Her fascination with the ocean led her to a small coastal town, where she became particularly interested in the local kina (sea urchin) population. Hannah's research on the kina's role in maintaining the delicate balance of the marine ecosystem earned her international recognition. She worked closely with the indigenous Maori community, learning about their traditional methods of sustainable kina harvesting. Together, they developed innovative conservation strategies that helped restore the kina population and preserve the marine environment. Hannah's dedication to her work and her collaboration with the local community made her a respected and beloved figure in the town.",
